<title>UK: Brown says no change to income tax rates.</title>
<headline>Brown says no change to income tax rates.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown said in his budget on Wednesday that there would be no changes to income tax rates.  </p>
<p>&quot;In this budget I have no changes to make to income tax either at the basic or top rate,&quot; he said in this budget speech.</p>
<p>This is in line with the government's election pledge not to raise income tax rates in the course of this Parliament.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom + 44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
